# Shell scripts and container entrypoints MUST keep LF endings.
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites them to CRLF on
# checkout; bash then fails with confusing errors ($'\r': command not found, or a
# syntax error on a script that is fine everywhere else). Harvis is meant to be
# cloned by strangers, so this cannot be left to each user's git config.
*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
Dockerfile.*    text eol=lf
*.bash          text eol=lf

# Files read by Linux containers verbatim — keep LF so mounted copies parse.
*.yaml          text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.sql           text eol=lf
.env.example    text eol=lf
